Fixed. The bug was on the old line 7: `b.url === inc.url` compared URLs as raw strings, which is case-sensitive. Hostnames are case-insignificant per RFC 3986, so `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` and `https://example.com/a` are the same URL but were treated as different.

**Change** (`src/import_merge.ts`):
- Added `sameUrl(a, b)` helper that parses both strings via the `URL` constructor and compares protocol, host, pathname, search, and hash.
- Replaced `b.url === inc.url` with `sameUrl(b.url, inc.url)` in the `.find()` call.

The `URL` constructor lowercases the hostname during parsing, so `new URL("https://EXAMPLE.com/a").host` normalizes to `"example.com"` — case mismatches are now correctly detected as duplicates.


